/T (Baltimore respondents face significant challenges in their music careers, with 19% struggling with rent or mortgage payments and 84% citing low or uncertain pay as a major issue. Rising costs of living and stagnant pay rates are top concerns for 37% and 30% of respondents, respectively. Venue/Presenters also report challenges with fan behavior post-COVID and talent costs, with 27% and 23% rating these as significant challenges. While 65% of respondents do not face affordability issues, a notable portion of the music community still grapples with financial insecurity.)
